#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0155 expect=noViolation domain=APAE
#note "APAE is a legal Associated Persons dataset: DOMAIN is exactly 4 characters, begins with `AP`, and its 2-character suffix `AE` is a published SDTM domain abbreviation. Both disjuncts of the Check are false, so the rule is silent. ⚠⚠ The `#library codelist-terms DOMAIN` line MUST carry real 2-letter SDTM SUBMISSION VALUES (`AE`, `CM`, `VS`, `LB`), never NCI C-codes — `suffix(DOMAIN, 2)` yields `AE`, and it is looked up in exactly this list. The CDISC-CG0001 / CORE-000929 fixtures are the pattern to FOLLOW, not to avoid: they were re-authored in ca63ebf5 and now split the three channels properly — submission values on `#library codelist-terms`, NCI C-codes on `#library codelist-term-ccodes`, the codelist's own ccode / preferred term on `#library codelist-meta`. Copy that shape if this fixture ever needs C-codes. ⚠ The rule's operation declares `returntype=\"value\"` and coreJ HONOURS the parameter (ca63ebf5): `codelist_terms` yields term submission values by contract, not because the parameter is ignored. This scenario is the net that makes a regression visible if either half changes. See plans/PLAN-codelist-terms-returntype.md."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-3
#library codelist-terms DOMAIN AE CM VS LB
dataset APAE label="Associated Persons Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col APID    type=Char label="Associated Persons Identifier"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | APAE | AP-701-1015
